{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואבדיל אתכם מן העמים", :translit "va'avdil etchem min ha'amim", :gloss "and I shall separate you from the peoples"} {:he "איש או אשה כי יהיה בהם אוב או ידעוני", :translit "ish o ishah ki yihyeh bahem ov o yidde'oni", :gloss "a man or a woman when there shall be in them an ov or a yidde'oni"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parashiyot: the juxtaposition of adjacent passages supplies the rationale — separation from nations means Israel needs no mediums because the Shekhinah dwells among them"}], :frame {:text "The method of reading adjacent Torah passages together (semikhut parashiyot) is a standard hermeneutical technique among the rabbis. The concept that the nations of the world resort to necromancy because they lack access to prophetic revelation is discussed in the Talmud (Sanhedrin 65a), which contrasts Israel's access to prophets with the nations' reliance on practitioners of ov and yidde'oni.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:27" "Sanhedrin 65a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parashiyot: the juxtaposition of adjacent passages supplies the rationale — separation from nations means Israel needs no mediums because the Shekhinah dwells among them", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:38.234199467Z", :model "glm-5.2"}